% M18-coverage-T9 step 2 (D-0269): ONE trace line per maximal removed gap. Element E1
% (i over [1, 2, 9, 10]) removes c's gap 3..8 in one bulk entry, whose line is
% `~c_ge_3 \/ c_ge_9`. Element E2 reads c as its INDEX: r's values 2..4 lose every
% support (3 is carried by c's gap positions only), so E2 removes r's gap 2..4, and that
% line is RUP only through c's gap line (the sweep over c climbs from c >= 3 to c >= 9
% through it; E1's rows cannot make that step). d = 1 then confines r to 2..4 and fails,
% so the trace is written under a decision over a satisfiable model. The mutation lane
% of test_mutation.ml shrinks c's gap at either end and asserts the r line is refused.
var 1..4: i :: output_var;
var 1..10: c :: output_var;
var 1..5: r :: output_var;
var 0..1: d :: output_var;
constraint array_int_element(i, [1, 2, 9, 10], c);
constraint array_int_element(c, [1, 1, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 5, 5], r);
constraint int_lin_le([1, 10], [r, d], 14);
constraint int_lin_le([-1, 10], [r, d], 8);
solve :: int_search([d, i], input_order, indomain_max, complete) satisfy;
